00:46:16,799 --> 00:46:22,799
Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery (or simply Austin Powers) is
a 1997 American spy comedy film directed by Jay Roach.

14
00:49:50,400 --> 00:49:56,400
It is the first installment in the Austin Powers series.

15
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:30,000
It stars franchise co-producer and writer Mike Myers, playing
the roles of Austin Powers and his arch enemy Dr.

16
00:56:57,599 --> 00:57:03,599
Supporting roles are played by Elizabeth Hurley, Robert
Wagner, Seth Green, and Michael York.

17
01:00:31,199 --> 01:00:37,199
The film is a parody of the James Bond films and other popular culture from the 1960s, centering on a flamboyant, promiscuous secret agent and a
criminal mastermind arch-nemesis, who go into and come out of cryostasis at the same time as each other as their conflict spans decades.

18
01:04:04,799 --> 01:04:10,799
The film, which cost $16.5 million to produce, was released on May 2, 1997.

19
01:07:38,400 --> 01:07:44,400
It received generally positive reviews from critics
and grossed $67 million worldwide.

20
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:18,000
It is now regarded as one of the best comedy films of all time, ranking
42nd on Bravo's "100 Funniest Movies of All Time" list.

21
01:14:45,599 --> 01:14:51,599
The film spawned two sequels, Austin Powers: The Spy Who Shagged
Me (1999) and Austin Powers in Goldmember (2002).

22
01:18:19,199 --> 01:18:25,199
In the years following Austin Powers in Goldmember, Myers has discussed the possibility of
a fourth film, though as of 2026 nothing official has come to fruition.

23
01:21:52,800 --> 01:21:58,800
The film explores themes of undercover, missile,
spy, group therapy, secret agent.

24
01:25:26,399 --> 01:25:32,399
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
